// Static, hand-researched (WebSearch-verified, then independently fact-
// checked by a second pass) reference details for each of the 66 KJV
// books -- the origin/meaning of its name, its traditional author and
// approximate date of writing (hedged honestly where real scholarly
// disagreement exists, never asserted as settled fact when it is not),
// and a neutral, factual synopsis of its content. This is entirely local,
// bundled data, not fetched -- bibleApi.js only ever returns verse TEXT,
// never book-level detail like this, so there is no live source for any
// of it. Written fresh in neutral, encyclopedia-style language, never
// copied or closely paraphrased from any specific copyrighted study
// Bible's own front matter. Keyed by the exact same book-name spelling
// BIBLE_BOOKS (utils/citations.js) and BOOK_CHAPTER_COUNTS/BOOK_SECTIONS
// (utils/bibleBooks.js) already use, so a lookup by browseBook in
// ScriptureIndexPanel.jsx never has to worry about a spelling mismatch.
