    synopsis: "Genesis opens the Bible with an account of creation and primeval history—Adam and Eve, Cain and Abel, the flood, and the Tower of Babel—before narrowing to the family history of Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and Joseph. It establishes the covenant God makes with Abraham and his descendants as the foundation for Israel's identity. The Joseph narrative closes the book by explaining how the family came to settle in Egypt, setting up the story of Exodus. Throughout, the book moves from universal beginnings to a single family's story, emphasizing promise, covenant, and providence.",
